cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Cortical-Column Memory: A Thousand-Brains-Inspired Memory and Consensus Architecture for Resource-Constrained Multi-Agent Systems"
message: "If you use this research artifact, please cite the v0.1.0 protocol release."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Booth
    given-names: James
    affiliation: Independent researcher
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-03
repository-code: "https://github.com/jmsbooth/agentic-cortical-column-memory"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A systems architecture and preregistered evaluation protocol for explicit
  modular memory, navigable reference frames, distributed hypotheses, active
  evidence gathering, and structured consensus in resource-constrained
  multi-agent systems. The release contains a dependency-free reference
  implementation and deterministic validation harness; the registered campaign
  is pending.
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - agent memory
  - test-time compute
  - reproducibility
  - reference frames
  - consensus
